<p id="mwBR0">The Clippers shot 0 of 12 in the fourth quarter on shots that could have tied the game or taken the lead. That is the most such attempts without a make in the fourth quarter of a game over the last 25 postseasons. During the last 8 seconds of the game when the Clippers trailed by 1 point, there was a controversial call where <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicolas_Batum" title="Nicolas Batum" id="mwBR4">Nicolas Batum</a> of the Clippers deflected the ball off the finger tips of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cameron_Payne" title="Cameron Payne" id="mwBR8">Cameron Payne</a> of the Suns, but the ball was given to the Suns. There was no review of the play despite a heavy plea from the Clippers.</p>
